                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The patient shows mildly decreased glomerular filtration rate (GFR) at 57 mL/min/1.73m², below the normal range, indicating stage 3a chronic kidney disease. This suggests moderate reduction in kidney function. Clinical correlation and monitoring of renal function, as well as assessment for underlying causes and potential complications, are recommended.</td>
